

A list is:

An ordered
Mutable
Collection of references to objects

Example:
a = [10, 20, 30, 40]

List khud values store nahi karti
List objects ke addresses (references) store karti hai.

How Python stores a list in memory
(C array of references)

Internally Python list ≈ C array

List (array)
+----+----+----+----+
| *  | *  | *  | *  |
+----+----+----+----+
  |    |    |    |
  v    v    v    v
 10   20   30   40   (objects in heap)


✔ Array ke andar pointers (references)
✔ Objects heap memory me kahin bhi ho sakte hain
✔ List ka array contiguous hota hai, objects nahi


Creation of list 

normal way 
list = [1,2,3,4,5]

using list()
l = list("thisislist")
